Adapted material
----------------

The battle scene (Battle Scene: OVERWORLD, src/scene/) adapts Emerald 3DS by Zallax and
contributors (https://github.com/ZallaxDev/emerald-3ds), licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: its 3D
battle's stage pose and entrance glide, and its battle stage search (3ds_port/src/voxel/
voxel_battle.c and ctr_voxel.c). Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE; one camera model, in the
battle canvas's own pixels, for both the search and the drawing; flat ground; no field-of-view
zoom in the glide; the world drawn by WoobleView's battle composite under the game's own
sprites and UI.

The battle scene's trees (src/scene/trees.lua, assets/scene/trees.png) adapt Emerald 3DS's
voxel trees (3ds_port/src/voxel/voxel_tree.c) and use its tree artwork
(3ds_port/assets/voxel/trees/, packed by tools/pack_trees.py at the places its own packer puts
them). Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE; a plain RGBA atlas instead of the 3DS's tiled
RGBA5551; AgainstRock and EmitGround worked out ahead of the drawing, off the battle's own cell
window, a trunk's ground on a slope laid from a slot of the relief's atlas; voxel_battle.c's
ReadCell tree heights and KindOf ported to the stage search, a Kanto game's tall grass also its
Cycling Road's; a secondary tileset told by the engine's tileset pair name.

The battle scene's buildings (src/scene/models/kernel.lua, src/scene/models/specs.lua,
src/scene/buildings.lua) adapt Emerald 3DS's building models: the modelling primitives of
3ds_port/scripts/voxel_building.py, the building specs of voxel_building_specs.py (every
reading of a building's drawing, its numbers unchanged), and how gen_voxel_buildings.py composes
a building's art and finds where it stands (find_placements, with same_building_pixels,
_sign_metatiles over gen_voxel_sign_masks.py's sign_record, _canonical_at and the `anywhere`
flag), a cell two placements hold answered by the first as voxel_building.c's CellGridOf does.
Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE and run in the game on the player's own tilesets instead of
offline; no proofs, previews or texture pages; only the
specs built from explicit parts, from flat faces over their drawing (with_ring, Grown, Card)
and from solids cut to their drawing (Volume, HeightSolid, own_bands, ProjSection, ProjHull,
ProjCanopy, Mound, VoxelLathe and BakedLathe: src/scene/models/solids.lua and solid_specs.lua)
so far. Rustboro's fountain's jet follows the game's tile animation as gen_voxel_buildings.py's
"live" texels do, its frames read from the engine's own animation banks. The ground laid under a
building (src/scene/buildings.lua's groundPlan) adapts gen_voxel_buildings.py's placement_ground,
patched_cells, placement_patches and bare_quarters with its patch_cells, patch_own, ground_fixed,
cell_ground and relief_bare flags, and voxel_building.c's VoxelBuildings_CellAt and
VoxelBuildings_BareVariant, read over the battle's own maps. Lilycove's beacon (lilycove_beacon)
and the flat drawing of a bare cell off the relief come from Emerald 3DS's dev branch (commit
de38764, after v0.5.0).

Fortree's tree houses, bridges and palms (src/scene/models/fortree.lua) adapt Emerald 3DS's
3ds_port/scripts/voxel_fortree.py (treehouse, LeafRoof, ProjPoly, bridge_planks, bridge_cell,
palm) and their specs in voxel_building_specs.py, with gen_voxel_buildings.py's rule that a spec
with owned cells stands only at its repeat_at places. Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE and run
in the game; the deck table (who is lifted onto a deck) is kept for an overworld view, unused by
the battle scene, as its battle stage search does not use it either.

Route 110's Seaside Cycling Road (src/scene/models/bridge.lua) adapts Emerald 3DS's
3ds_port/scripts/voxel_bridge.py (the road read off its drawing, its faces, corners, merge,
dressed sides and blocks) and its "cycling_road" spec in voxel_building_specs.py. Changes:
rewritten in Lua for LOVE and read in the game from the player's own cartridge, a slice a frame,
its blocks kept in the mod's cache on one texture; its deck table and shadow footprints (and
gen_voxel_buildings.py's cell_footprints for every other model) are kept for an overworld view,
unused by the battle scene.

The battle scene's rooms (src/scene/models/interiors.lua and interior_specs.lua) adapt Emerald
3DS's 3ds_port/scripts/gen_voxel_buildings.py (interior_specs - a room cut into its walls and
furniture, a model each - with its helpers: _inside, fill_hidden, find_supports, auto_leave,
support_left, outline_trim, leg_split, plain_side, side_image, slab_side, table_plan,
table_parts, pick_side, ball_fit, lathe_fit, dome_fit, post_parts, decal_cells, floor_under, the
reuse of a piece in every room that draws it again, and find_placements' rules for a room's
pieces), the interior specs of voxel_building_specs.py (all of its rooms, in its order) and
voxel_building.py's ProjDome,
ProjLathe, ProjRun and Ribbon
(src/scene/models/solids.lua). Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE and run in the game on the
player's own cartridge, the rooms read in the background and kept in the mod's cache; no proofs
or lint; the frames of an animated piece read off the engine's own animation banks.

The battle scene's rocks and boulders (src/scene/props.lua) adapt Emerald 3DS's
3ds_port/scripts/voxel_props.py (its objects and their finder) and gen_voxel_buildings.py's
prop_specs (a model per offset and variant, a Mound on the cells' own ground, standing whatever
else stands there). Changes: found in
the game, map by map, around each battle; the flags' cloth follows the game's animation through
the engine's own animation banks.

The battle scene's hedges, fences, curbs, railings and walls (src/scene/models/components.lua,
src/scene/models/fence.lua, the Relief and Decal primitives in src/scene/models/kernel.lua) and
Rustboro's office blocks (the kits in src/scene/models/specs.lua) adapt Emerald 3DS's
`components` and `kit` specs and how gen_voxel_buildings.py builds them (component_specs,
piece_spec, kit_specs, close_gaps, trim_outline, join_corners, fill_behind, pick_side,
seam_art, flank_band, kept_by_others), its Relief and PlanPrism primitives (voxel_building.py)
and its fence builder (voxel_fence.py). Changes: run in the game on the window around the
battle (a run reaching past it ends at its edge); colours compared at the GBA's 5 bits a
channel.

The battle scene's signposts (src/scene/signs.lua) adapt Emerald 3DS's sign masks and sign
solids (3ds_port/scripts/voxel_sign_mask.py, gen_voxel_sign_masks.py, src/voxel/voxel_sign.c,
the signpost role of voxel_cells.py, with its rules for which cells are posts). Changes: read in
the game over the window around the battle (the engine's sign events, warps and drawings), drawn
from a texture of their own.

The battle scene's terrain relief (src/scene/relief.lua) adapts Emerald 3DS's relief file format
and runtime (3ds_port/src/voxel/voxel_relief.c: lattices, cut tiles, seam steps) and how its mesh
builder and atlas draw a lifted cell (voxel_mesh_builder.c: the cell's drawing on its lattice,
cut tiles' flat layers and run-on ground, cliff walls, a back's north face; voxel_atlas.c: a cut
tile's cleared background), and the border round the map (src/scene/render.lua and init.lua:
voxel_mesh_builder.c's VoxelMesh_EmitBorder, BorderWaterLevel, VoxelMesh_BorderLevel,
EmitBorderSteps and EmitBorderNorth - its courses, steps and north walls, a belt laid as its
map's drawing, the hand marks' edge fills in place of the border block - and EmitSeamSkirt with
SeamEdge, the walls from a map's edge up to the belt or down to a lower map beside it). Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE; no
lighting; one texture of the drawings a battle's window lays.

The relief solver (src/scene/relief_solve.lua, relief_art.lua, relief_input.lua,
relief_drawn.lua, relief_shape.lua, relief_cuts.lua, relief_world.lua) adapts Emerald 3DS's
gen_voxel_relief.py whole (3ds_port/scripts: the ledges, the drawn mountains read off their
pixels, the world's placement of the maps, the cut tiles and cell shapes, its export) with the
drawings composed as voxel_art.py and dump_region_art.py compose them and the objects of
voxel_props.py; its terraces (src/scene/relief_terraces.lua, relief_terraces_fit.lua,
relief_terraces_out.lua) adapt voxel_terraces.py whole. Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE,
run in the game once over the player's own cartridge data instead of offline, sliced a few
milliseconds a frame; Python's own arithmetic and ordering (its hash-ordered sets, compensated
sums, rounding) reproduced where the result depends on them, so the bytes come out the same.

Which layout a map is drawn with (src/scene/world.lua's settle) adapts Emerald 3DS's
src/voxel/voxel_world.c (FillInstance, NeighbourLayoutId and its sLayoutSwaps): a neighbour drawn
with the layout its script swaps in. Changes: the engine keeps no layout id for the current map,
so the layout swapped into it is the one whose cells the map draws.

The scene's light: src/scene/light.lua adapts Emerald 3DS's src/voxel/ctr_voxel.c (the
VoxelLight struct, BaseLightFor, LightMix, FogLight, SetGrade, MakeDapple, DappleFrame,
DappleUniforms, BrightenCrowns), src/voxel/voxel_grade.c (the texture grade) and
src/voxel/voxel_world.c (VoxelWorld_Weather, _WeatherAmount, _FogDensity, _Lightning);
src/scene/lighting.lua adapts src/voxel/voxel_lighting.c whole (the face term, the cast shadows,
contact darkening, LightFace, the relief lattice, ModelShade) and voxel_relief.c's BuildSurface,
SurfaceAt and SurfaceTop, and src/scene/relief.lua takes voxel_mesh_builder.c's ReliefFace,
SpanLinear and the builder's lighting flags; src/scene/sunfx.lua adapts ctr_voxel.c's MakeRays,
DrawRays, DrawMotes, MoteRandom and the battle intro's impact, and src/3ds_video.c's
VoxelBloomPrepare and VoxelBloomCompose; src/scene/weather.lua adapts ctr_voxel.c's MakeFog,
DrawBanks, MakeWeather, WeatherOffset, DrawWeather and the weather kinds, and
src/voxel/voxel_weather.v.pica; src/scene/screenfx.lua adapts src/3ds_video.c's VoxelDiorama,
DioramaTap, BattleIntroZoomTap, BattleIntroBlur, BattleIntroAtmosphere, BattleIntroFlash and
BattleIntroBars, and ctr_voxel.c's BattleCamera intro values; src/gen3.lua's sandstorm hook
adapts their patch to battle_anim_rock.c (AnimTask_LoadSandstormBackground) and 3ds_video.c's
CtrBattle_Sandstorm. Changes: rewritten in Lua for LOVE; the casters read
off the battle's own cell window; a ray marches every point up to the casters' ceiling (their
cell skips and block bounds change no answer); the grade, the dapples and the haze worked out
per pixel; the bloom made from a canvas halved to their screen's width first; the weather's
particles drawn by a GLSL shader; the blurs sampled from a copy of the world at their screen's
size, the zoom blur about the camera's target; the cinema bars drawn over WoobleView's
composite; the speed lines and vignette run to the canvas's foot beside a text box narrower than
the view; the weather read
from the engine's copy of the game's weather state; their day/night cycle (tint, moonlight and
clock sun, behind their "day_night" setting, off by default) is not ported.

The relief's last passes (src/scene/relief_post.lua) adapt Emerald 3DS's sea ramps and cut feet
(3ds_port/scripts/gen_voxel_relief.py) and its hand corrections (voxel_relief_fixes.py: how
relief.bin is read and written, how the corrections apply), and assets/scene/relief_fixes.json
is Emerald 3DS's own hand corrections (3ds_port/assets/voxel/relief_fixes.json: levels, pieces,
bases, belts and edge fills set by hand, cell by cell, for 39 maps; no data of the cartridge's).
Changes: rewritten in Lua, the maps read from the game instead of pret's files; the corrections
file minified (its contents and key order unchanged).

Pokemon is (c) Nintendo, Game Freak and Creatures. WoobleView contains none of their content.

